# Work-tracker scope — this repository does not exist there

This project (`logbook.rocks`, `KavehRS/logbook.rocks`, climb reports, news, articles, SEO, Cloudflare for this site, Cursor agent runs on this repo) is **out of scope** for any employer or work tracker.

## Never, unless the owner’s message in that same turn explicitly names this repository and asks to include it

Do not put any of this into:

- Azure, Azure DevOps, Azure Boards, work items, PRs, wikis, or pipelines
- گزارش کار, timesheets, weekly/daily status, standup notes, or similar work reports
- any other company’s tracker, ticket, or status document

Treat the work as if it is not there. Do not summarize it. Do not link it. Do not list commits, PRs, agent runs, or “personal site” as a line item.

## Silence about the omission

If writing a work report or filling Azure: **do not mention this repository at all.**

Do **not** write that the owner asked to exclude it.
Do **not** write that something was omitted, filtered, private, personal, or out of scope.
Do **not** add a footnote, parenthetical, or “سایر موارد ذکر نشد.”

The report should look as if this project does not exist.

## The only exception

Include this repository **only** when the owner’s request for that Azure item or گزارش کار **directly says** to include it (names this repo / logbook.rocks / this site and tells you to bring it). A general “گزارش کار بده” or “آپدیت آژور” is **not** that exception.
